  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Segregated Witness (SegWit) is a protocol upgrade, activated on Bitcoin as a backwards-compatible soft fork, that moves the witness data \u2014 the digital signatures authorising spends \u2014 out of the main transaction body into a separate structure. By segregating signatures, it fixes transaction malleability, since the transaction identifier no longer depends on mutable signature data, and effectively increases block capacity through a block-weight accounting scheme. SegWit also created the foundation for second-layer protocols such as the Lightning Network and enabled later script upgrades.",
